@prefix backlog: <http://example.org/backlog#> .
@prefix ex:      <http://example.org/sen0414-ch19ch20-lineage#> .
@prefix owl:     <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:     <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

<http://example.org/sen0414-ch19ch20-lineage> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "Fresh narrow lineage: SEN0414 Chapters 19 and 20"@en ;
    owl:versionInfo "1.7.0" ; owl:versionIRI <http://example.org/sen0414-ch19ch20-lineage/1.7.0> ; dcterms:identifier "sen0414_ch19ch20_lineage" ;
    rdfs:comment "1.7.0 (2026-11-12): Owner questioned stories 5 and 6 of chapter 20; draft v1.0.1 replaces the Gmail story with an IMAP story and rewrites the AT&T story with reasons and alternatives. Approval gate stays Ready."@en .

ex:TK8_DraftVerify_Ch20 backlog:hasAuditNote "Re-read by WebSearch on 2026-11-12: Tomlinson 1971 and @; RFC 821 Postel August 1982, obsoleted by RFC 2821; SMS 3 Dec 1992; AT&T gateway ended 17 June 2025 (AT&T gives no reason; reasons in the draft are marked as commentators' judgements). Defects fixed: first-spam recipient count differs by source (stated in the draft); on the owner's question the Gmail story (code name Caribou, 1 GB) was dropped as weakly tied to the chapter and replaced by the IMAP story (Mark Crispin 1986, RFC 1064 in 1988 and RFC 1176 in 1990, from Wikipedia and imap.org, both answering 200). Repeat scan of the story scripts of chapters 1 to 19 for IMAP and Crispin: no hit. Same agent as the writer, so not independent; the owner may overrule." .
ex:Obs1_Draft_Ch20_Revision a backlog:MetricObservation ; backlog:observationForMetric ex:Metric_Obj8_StoriesChecked ;
    backlog:observedValue 0 ; backlog:observedAt "2026-11-12T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    rdfs:comment "Measured: the replacement IMAP story of chapter 20 was compared by keyword with the stories of chapters 1 to 19; 0 repeats."@en .
